# Approach
- Odd number of `?` → Alice wins immediately.
- Even number of `?` → Calculate the fixed difference and compare it with `9 × (rightQ - leftQ) / 2`.

## Elaborate Final Condition:
Therefore the core line is:

`return diff != 9 * (rightQ - leftQ) / 2;`

It means:

After considering the fixed digits and the question-mark imbalance, if Bob cannot make the final difference exactly zero, Alice wins.

If:

`(leftSum - rightSum) == 9 * (rightQ - leftQ) / 2`

then Bob can force:

`leftSum == rightSum`

so:

`false`

Otherwise:

`true`

# Complexity
- Time complexity: $$O(n)$$

- Space complexity: $$O(1)$$

# Code
```java []
class Solution {
    public boolean sumGame(String num) {
        int n = num.length();

        int leftSum = 0;
        int rightSum = 0;
        int leftQ = 0;
        int rightQ = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < n / 2; i++) {
            char ch = num.charAt(i);

            if (ch == '?') {
                leftQ++;
            } else {
                leftSum += ch - '0';
            }
        }

        for (int i = n / 2; i < n; i++) {
            char ch = num.charAt(i);

            if (ch == '?') {
                rightQ++;
            } else {
                rightSum += ch - '0';
            }
        }

        // Odd number of '?' means Alice gets one extra turn.
        if ((leftQ + rightQ) % 2 == 1) {
            return true;
        }

        return (leftSum - rightSum) != 9 * (rightQ - leftQ) / 2;
    }
}
```
